  "raw": {
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Instructor-of-Chemistry_R00117441": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor or Instructor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor or Instructor of Chemistry     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Mathematics and Physical Sciences (Prakash Ghimire (00042323))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Chemistry   Job Description: The Department of Chemistry and Physics at Louisiana State University at Alexandria invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Chemistry. This is a 9-month position to begin in January 2027. This position focuses on providing high-quality instruction in undergraduate chemistry courses both on campus and online. The ideal candidate will hold a Ph.D. in Chemistry and have demonstrated teaching experience in Organic Chemistry in both face-to-face and online instructional formats. Candidates should also be prepared to teach a range of other chemistry courses. Opportunities exist to develop and teach additional upper-level courses aligned with the candidate’s area of expertise. Responsibilities: Typical duties include but are not limited to:   Develops and teaches undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses as assigned, both in-person and online. Maintains high standards of instruction and uses effective teaching methods to support student success. Engages in scholarly activities and mentors undergraduate chemistry research Maintains regular office hours and provides accessible student support. Advises students on academic progress and career opportunities. Participates in curriculum development, assessment, and program improvement Serves on University committees and participates in departmental and institutional activities. Performs other duties as assigned by the supervisor This position entails 60% teaching, 20% scholarly activities, and 20% community/university service. Application Instructions : Please submit application, uploading the following as a single PDF: (1) cover letter, (2) CV that includes contact information for three references, (3) teaching philosophy, (4) short statement on research interests and how you would incorporate undergraduate students, (5) unofficial transcripts.   Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired.   For questions or concerns regarding the status of your application or other details about the position, please contact hr@lsua.edu or 318-473-6401.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Application Instructions: Please submit application, uploading the following as a single PDF: (1) cover letter, (2) CV that includes contact information for three references, (3) teaching philosophy, (4) short statement on research interests and how you would incorporate undergraduate students, (5) unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 9, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Associate-Professor-of-Kinesiology_R00121147-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology:  Health and Physical Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Kinesiology: Health and Physical Education     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - HHS - Education (Arlene Andrepont Duos (00002657))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Faculty in Kinesiology for Health and Physical Education (Grades K-12) 9-Month Tenure-Track Position   The Kinesiology Program at Louisiana State University in Alexandria (LSUA) seeks applications for Assistant Professor of Kinesiology for Health and Physical Education (Grades K-12). Applicants should be strongly committed to excellence in teaching and to working in an environment that fosters diversity. Candidates need the ability to use technology effectively in teaching and learning to work collaboratively, to provide evidence of scholarly activity, and to demonstrate a commitment to public higher education.   The Kinesiology Program at LSUA invites applicants for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level. The program seeks an outstanding faculty member who will contribute to undergraduate programs focusing on basic aspects of kinesiology and health and physical education. The program offers core kinesiology courses taken by all kinesiology majors and four concentrations: health and physical education; health and fitness studies; sports management; and coaching and sport performance. The appointment will begin January 2027.   Assistant Professor Rank   Required Qualifications: ·         Master's degree in Health and Physical Education (or related area) from an accredited institution including 1& graduate hours in Health and Physical Education ·         Evidence of collaboration with local school systems, community agencies or other professionals ·         Evidence of the application of technology ·         Evidence of scholarly activities   Preferred Qualifications: ·         ABD or earned doctorate in the discipline from an accredited university ·         Experience with the delivery of instruction at the university level in online environments ·         University teaching experience ·         Coaching experience   Duties and Responsibilities: ·         Teach a variety of undergraduate kinesiology courses including coaching, health and physical education> and core courses ·         Collaborate with local school systems, community agencies, or other professionals ·         Continue professional development in the discipline via professional organization membership and research ·         Participate in faculty governance, committees, and other events/organizations on campus ·         Create an engaging learning environment that is effective and encourages student involvement and participation to stimulate earning ·         Participate in retention and recruitment of prospective students ·         Perform other responsibilities requested by administration Advise kinesiology, health and physical education students, and others as assigned     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Application Instructions: Please attach a Resume/CV, a cover letter, 3 references and unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. Please attach all transcripts to your application. A background check is required for hire. Questions or concerns about your application should be directed to LSUA Human Resources at (318) 473-6401 or hr@lsua.edu.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: October 2, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Instructor---Part-Time----Africana-Studies_R00120948": {
      "title": "Instructor - Part-Time  - Africana Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor - Part-Time - Africana Studies     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Liberal Arts (Brenda R Ellington (00009758))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Applicants must have a Master’s or Ph.D. degree in Music or Africana Studies or a related field with teaching experience preferred. Applicants should submit a letter of application detailing qualifications, a CV, unofficial transcripts, and three (3) letters of recommendation. Official transcripts, a Disclosure Statement, and a professional writing sample will be required prior to employment.  All application materials should be uploaded to the application.     Additional Job Description: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is seeking an adjunct in Africana Studies to teach in an online format the following 3 credit course as part of our Bachelor of General Studies in Africana Studies program: AFST 3030 – Black Musical Traditions. This course acts as a survey of Black African musical traditions, examining West & Central African musical ideas and tracing the spread and manifestation of these ideas in the variety of music of the Atlantic World. Responsibilities: ·         Developing a class syllabus ·         Ordering required textbooks before start of class ·         Preparing lectures or teaching pdfs and student assignments ·         Being available for student conferences ·         Presenting instruction based on online course description ·         Submitting attendance reporting ·         Evaluating student performance on assignments and exams in a timely manner ·         Submitting midterm and final grades according to university regulations ·         Providing student evaluation of the course ·         Building positive rapport with students and faculty Physical Requirements: ·         Ability to instruct online in Moodle (an online course in how to teach online and how to use Moodle may be required) ·         Availability for student conferences ·         Ability to grade assignments and examinations Applicants must have a Master’s or Ph.D. degree in Music or Africana Studies or a related field with teaching experience preferred. Applicants should submit a letter of application detailing qualifications, a CV, unofficial transcripts, and three (3) letters of recommendation. Official transcripts, a Disclosure Statement, and a professional writing sample will be required prior to employment.  All application materials should be uploaded to the application. Competencies: None Special Instructions:     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 23, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Assistant-Professor-of-Communication-Studies_R00120333": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Communication Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Communication Studies     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Liberal Arts (Brenda R Ellington (00009758))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Communication Studies Position Type: Faculty Department: LSUA ASA - Liberal Arts (Brenda R Ellington (00009758)) Work Location: LSU - Alexandria Pay Grade: Academic Job Description: Assistant Professor of Communication Studies Department: Communication & Arts, College of Liberal Arts Position Title: Assistant Professor of Communication Studies Supervisor: Dean, College of Liberal Arts Purpose: The Communication Studies Program at Louisiana State University of Alexandria (the fastest growing university in the state of Louisiana) seeks an Assistant Professor to join a dynamic team to teach a range of undergraduate communication courses in a variety formats (face to face, hybrid, online). The successful candidate will be a communication generalist willing to teach both introductory and upper-level courses with special consideration given to a candidate's area of specialization. RESPONSIBILITIES: This position implies both competency in the discipline of Communication Studies as well as an enthusiasm for teaching and mentoring college students. LSUA is focused only on undergraduate education, and because of this, we place great emphasis on the scholarship of teaching. The successful candidate will be required to maintain a full-time annual teaching load, maintain involvement and interaction both with students and the university as a whole. At LSUA, we aren't afraid to work hard. We get involved, we set up our own tables, and we get excited about new dry erase markers. Academic rigor is a priority, but we're also looking for a team player who values collaboration and teamwork. Typical duties include but are not limited to: Plans and teaches courses as assigned Maintains flexibility and willingness to teach in a variety of environments Prepares syllabi, instructional materials, coordinates lectures, tests, and evaluates Maintains highest possible standards of classroom instruction Regularly keeps office hours and maintains willingness to be receptive to students both in person and through email Actively serves on university committees Actively participates in institutional meetings Demonstrates willingness to learn and enhance professional skills through regular professional development and other activities appropriate to higher education faculty Stays updated on new information and developments in field of instruction Assists with curriculum development Performs other duties as assigned by the supervisor MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master's degree in Communication or related field. Terminal degree and teaching experience preferred. Dependent upon qualifications, candidate may be hired as an Instructor or Assistant Professor; rank will be commensurate with qualifications.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Background check is required for hire. Questions or concerns about your application should be directed to LSUA Human Resources at 318-473-6401 or hr@lsua.edu. Please attach all transcripts to your application for proof of education     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 9, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified): October 26, 2026    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
