    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Assistant-Professor-of-Molecular-Biology--Genomics--or-Bioinformatics_R00117447": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Molecular Biology, Genomics, or Bioinformatics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Molecular Biology, Genomics, or Bioinformatics     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Biological Sciences (Nathan J Sammons (00007928))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: PURPOSE: The Department of Biological Sciences at Louisiana State University of Alexandria seeks a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor in Molecular Biology, Genomics, Bioinformatics, or a closely related field. The successful candidate will provide high-quality undergraduate instruction, develop an active research program involving undergraduate students, and contribute to the continued growth and development of the department's academic programs. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses in Molecular Biology, Genomics, Bioinformatics, Cell Biology, and other courses consistent with departmental needs and the candidate's expertise. Develop and maintain an active scholarly research program that engages undergraduate students. Provide academic advising, mentoring, and support to students through regular office hours and other communication channels. Develop and deliver high-quality instruction using effective and innovative teaching practices. Participate in curriculum development, assessment activities, accreditation efforts, and program review. Serve on departmental, college, and university committees. Collaborate with faculty to support student recruitment, retention, undergraduate research, and community outreach initiatives. Contribute to the continued development of biology degree programs, including emerging programs and online offerings as appropriate. Maintain appropriate records and complete university reporting requirements in a timely manner. Perform other duties as assigned by the department chair or supervisor. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Ph.D. in Molecular Biology, Genomics, Bioinformatics, Genetics, Cell Biology, Computational Biology, or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution by the date of appointment. Teaching Ability: Demonstrated potential for effective undergraduate teaching. Research Experience: Demonstrated potential for scholarly productivity and undergraduate research mentorship. Communication Skills: Strong oral, written, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Preferred Experience: Experience teaching undergraduate courses and laboratories in molecular biology, genetics, genomics, or bioinformatics. Preferred Experience: Experience involving undergraduate students in research activities. Technical Expertise: Experience with genomic data analysis, next- generation sequencing technologies, computational biology tools, or related methodologies. Technology Skills: Experience with online or hybrid instruction is preferred. Commitment to Student Success: Demonstrated commitment to student success and inclusive teaching practices.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Applicants should submit in one PDF file: • Letter of application addressing qualifications for the position • Curriculum vitae • Statement of teaching philosophy • Statement of research interests and plans for involving undergraduate students • Unofficial graduate transcripts • Contact information for three professional references Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 17, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Assistant-Professor-of-Information-Technology--Tenure-Track-_R00117446": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Information Technology (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Assistant Professor of Information Technology (Tenure-Track)     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Mathematics and Physical Sciences (Nathan J Sammons (00007928))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: PURPOSE: Louisiana State University at Alexandria (LSUA) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of lnformation Technology (IT). The successful candidate will provide high-quality instruction in undergraduate Information Technology courses and support related programs by teaching selected Computer Science and Cybersecurity courses in both face-to-face and online formats. LSUA is partnering with LSU Online to offer an accelerated Bachelor of Science degree in Information Technology. The successful candidate will play a vital role in the continued growth, development, and delivery of this program while contributing to the university's mission of academic excellence, student success, scholarship, and service. RESPONSIBILITIES: Typical duties include, but are not limited to: Teach undergraduate Information Technology courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. Teach selected undergraduate Computer Science and Cybersecurity courses as needed. Develop and maintain high-quality instructional materials and utilize effective teaching strategies that support student success. Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives . Maintain regular office hours and provide academic support and mentoring to students in person and electronically. Advise students regarding academic planning, degree completion, internships, and career pathways. Contribute to the growth and success ofLSUA's Information Technology program, including support of the LSU Online partnership. Maintain an active program of scholarly, professional, and/or creative activity consistent with expectations for tenure-track faculty. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities, including committee assignments and faculty governance. Engage in professional development activities that support teaching effectiveness and disciplinary expertise. Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair, Dean, or University administration. QUALIFICATIONS: +     Required Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. in Information Technology (IT) or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered if the Ph.D. is completed by the time of hire. +     Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching undergraduate Information Technology, Computer Science and Cybersecurity courses. Demonstrated excellence in classroom and online teaching. Familiarity with or experience in online course development and delivery. Evidence of engagement in scholarly or professional development acti v ities     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Please submit applications through Workday by uploading the following as a single PDF: Detailed cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) Unofficial transcripts Contact information for three references Teaching Evaluations (if available) Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired. Application Deadline: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Start Date: January 11, 2027     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 17, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Instructor-of-Mathematics_R00117445": {
      "title": "Instructor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor of Mathematics     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Mathematics and Physical Sciences (Nathan J Sammons (00007928))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: PURPOSE: Louisiana State University at Alexandria (LSUA) invites applications for a Full-Time Instructor of Mathematics position. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to teach a wide range of undergraduate mathematics courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. The department is especially interested in candidates who are committed to excellence in teaching and who can provide high-quality instruction in general education mathematics courses. LSUA is partnering with LSU Online to offer a Bachelor of Science degree in Mathematics. The successful candidate will play a vital role in the continued growth, development, and delivery of this program while contributing to the university's mission of academic excellence, student success, and service. RESPONSIBILITIES: Typical duties include, but are not limited to: Teach undergraduate Mathematics courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. Develop and maintain high-quality instructional materials and utilize effective teaching strategies that support student success. Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic support and mentoring to students in person and electronically. Advise students regarding academic planning, degree completion, internships, and career pathways. Contribute to the growth and success of LSUA's Mathematics program, including support of the LSU Online partnership. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities, including committee assignments and faculty governance. Engage in professional development activities that support teaching effectiveness and disciplinary experti s e. Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair, Dean, or University administration. QUALIFICATIONS: +  Required Qualifications : Master's degree in mathematics or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution. Candidates holding a graduate degree in another discipline with at least 18 graduate semester credit hours in Mathematics will also be considered. +  Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching undergraduate Mathematics courses. Demonstrated excellence in classroom and online teaching . Familiarity with or experience in online course development and delivery. Evidence of engagement in scholarly or professional development activities     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Please uploading the following to your application as a single PDF: Detailed cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) Unofficial transcripts Contact information for three references Teaching Evaluations Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired. Application Deadline: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Start Date: August 16, 2027     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 17, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Instructor-of-Biology_R00117442": {
      "title": "Instructor of Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Instructor of Biology     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Biological Sciences (Nathan J Sammons (00007928))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: PURPOSE: Louisiana State University of Alexandria (LSUA) invites applications for a full-time Instructor of Biology position. This is a nine-month, non-remote position. The selected candidate will primarily teach Human Anatomy and Physiology courses, general education biology courses for non-science majors, and other courses as departmental needs arise. The instructor will support student success through effective teaching, course development, advising, and service to the department and university. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach undergraduate courses in Human Anatomy and Physiology and general biology in face-to-face and online formats. Teach general education biology courses for non- majors. Develop and deliver lectures, laboratory activities, assignments, and assessments. Develop online biology courses in collaboration with LSU Online as needed. Develop syllabi and instructional materials aligned with course objectives. Evaluate student performance through assignments, examinations, and other assessment methods. Provide support to students through office hours, tutoring, advising, and communication. Collaborate with colleagues to enhance curriculum and instructional quality. Participate in departmental meetings, committees, and service activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Graduate degree with at least 18 graduate credit hours in Human Anatomy and Physiology or a related biological science field. Experience: Teaching experience, preferably at the undergraduate level in biology. Teaching Ability: Demonstrated ability to effectively teach and engage students from diverse backgrounds. Technology Skills: Experience using learning management systems and instructional technologies. Commitment to Excellence: Commitment to teaching excellence and student success. Communication Skills: Strong oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Application Instructions: Application Instructions: Please submit application, uploading the following as a single PDF: (1) cover letter, (2) CV that includes contact information for three references, (3) teaching philosophy, (4) short statement on research interests and how you would incorporate undergraduate students, (5) unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired. Official transcripts, three letters of recommendation, and background check are required before a candidate can be hired.     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: July 17, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
    },
    "https://lsu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/LSU/job/LSU---Alexandria/Aviation-Instructor-Program-Coordinator_R00113845": {
      "title": "Aviation Instructor/Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Us: Louisiana State University of Alexandria is a publicly supported institution that provides undergraduate level college education to the citizens of Central Louisiana. The university is a unit of the LSU System and operates under the auspices of the Louisiana Board of Regents. LSUA is located in Rapides Parish. All Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Aviation Instructor/Program Coordinator     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUA ASA - Department of Academic Affairs (Eamon Gerald Halpin (00011143))     Work Location: LSU - Alexandria     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: Purpose: To serve as an instructor and program coordinator in the Aviation Program Responsibilities: Teach 12 hours of aviation courses, including ground courses, at both lower and upper levels. Assist in academic advising of aviation students and monitoring their progress towards meeting both degree requirements and FAA certification requirements. Assist in monitoring effectiveness of aviation curriculum and associated courses and contribute ideas for improvement as needed. Contribute to development and implementation of initiatives to recruit new students. Contribute to efforts to establish strong relationships with other aviation-related organizations, companies, and school operating in the region. Serve on university committees as needed. Provide service to community as needed. Qualifications: Master's degree in Aviation or Bachelor's degree in Aviation with at least 15 years of instructor experience (CFI, CFII, MEI) with a reputable flight school. Strong communication skills. Ability to motivate and engage with students. Self-motivated, cooperative, flexible, creative.     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Please attach a Resume/CV, a cover letter, 3 references and unofficial transcripts. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. Please attach all transcripts to your application. A background check is required for hire. Questions or concerns about your application should be directed to LSUA Human Resources at (318) 473-6401 or hr@lsua.edu.     Posting Date: April 7, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSUA offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!     Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUA is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSU Human Resources Management Office at 318-473-6401 or emailed hr@lsua.edu"
